{"availability":"available","full":"dagucloud/dagu","name":"dagu","description":"Self-hostable workflow orchestrator for teams whose main work isn't orchestration. Declarative YAML over your scripts, SSH commands, containers, etc; keep workflows separate from business logic. One binary, no database, runs on limited H/W resources. Alternative to Airflow / Cron / Job Scheduler.","category":"Business","language":"Go","stars":4251,"forks":358,"created":"2022-04-22T13:00:42Z","updated":"2026-10-04T03:13:37Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dagu.sh","topics":["agentic-workflows","ai-agents","ai-workflows","airflow-alternative","cron","dag","data-pipeline","devops","durable-execution","human-in-the-loop","job-scheduler","llm","mcp","mcp-gateway","mcp-server","self-hosted","task-automation","workflow-engine","workflow-orchestration","workflow-scheduler"],"demo":"https://dagu-demo-f5e33d0e.dagu.sh/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T10:32:25.986Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T10:32:25.986Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T10:32:25.986Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:41.024Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"curated-list","name":"Awesome Selfhosted","url":"https://github.com/awesome-selfhosted/awesome-selfhosted"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T09:36:41.024Z","stars":4247,"forks":358},{"at":"2026-10-04T10:32:25.986Z","stars":4251,"forks":358}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Dagu is a local-first workflow engine for operations and internal automation. It is open source and self-hostable: a single binary with a built-in Web UI, no external database or message broker, running on Linux, macOS, and Windows. Define DAGs in a declarative YAML format. It natively supports shell commands, Docker containers, Kubernetes Jobs, remote commands via SSH, and more through Dagu Actions.","Dagu turns existing scripts and runbooks into production workflows with scheduling, retries, human tasks, and run history. It runs where your data and credentials live: on-prem, air-gapped, edge, or cloud, and scales from a single node to a fleet of workers.","Orchestration is not your main work. You have scripts and containers that already work. You want a schedule, retries, dependencies, and a place to see logs. The usual options each have a cost:"],"features":["Single binary installation.","Self-contained: no external DBMS or message broker required.","Runs on Linux, macOS, and Windows.","Declarative YAML format for defining DAGs.","Compose reusable Sub-DAGs and run work in parallel with concurrency controls."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dagucloud/dagu/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c9b3e8041c63f4942feb5c19b9409ff24200c2bb91a71b87e6d0623f1ce71a3d","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T11:32:20.530Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T11:32:20.530Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T03:13:37Z","enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T07:02:19.420Z","latestRelease":{"name":"v2.18.1","tag":"v2.18.1","publishedAt":"2026-09-29T15:24:51Z","url":"https://github.com/dagucloud/dagu/releases/tag/v2.18.1"},"releaseCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T07:02:19.420Z","screenshots":[{"src":"previews/ca4182cc21fa76afa54da83c.jpg","kind":"demo","capturedAt":"2026-10-04T12:35:30.329Z","url":"https://dagu-demo-f5e33d0e.dagu.sh/"}],"overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T11:32:14.436Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Dagu is a local-first workflow engine for operations and internal automation. It is open source and self-hostable: a single binary with a built-in Web UI, no external database or message broker, running on Linux, macOS, and Windows. Define DAGs in a declarative YAML format. It natively supports shell commands, Docker containers, Kubernetes Jobs, remote commands via SSH, and more through Dagu Actions.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dagucloud/dagu/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The script installers run a guided wizard that 